      "content": "Protestant and Jewish conservatives generally oppose physician-assisted suicide by arguing it devalues human life and equates killing with a paternalism that only God should exercise. In contrast, religious liberals and groups like the Unitarians often support the practice as a legitimate ethical response to unbearable suffering and an act of compassion for the dying. This divide reflects a fundamental disagreement on whether the sanctity of life means preserving biological existence at all costs or allowing a dignified death when care ends.",
